    "title": "Lansdowne Man Faces Felony Threat Charges in Scranton Case - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tony Petras ,\n9 hours ago Richard Frisby, 47, of Lansdowne, faces felony charges of terroristic threats and witness intimidation involving his former girlfriend, Erica Vought, and James Pasco, according to the Scranton Times-Tribune. Citing a criminal complaint and affidavit, the newspaper reports that Frisby is being held at Lackawanna County Prison on $200,000 bail and has a preliminary hearing scheduled for Oct. 21 before Magisterial District Judge Paul Keeler. Read full article\n3",
